            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Jonathan S. Franklin (Petitioner), according to Jonathan S. Franklin (Petitioner), according to Jonathan S. Franklin (Petitioner), the case concerns a patent claim covering homocysteine testing that the petitioner says is infringed whenever a doctor looks at a homocysteine test result and thinks about a natural correlation."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Jonathan S. Franklin (Petitioner)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "8e14f67b26df95ffae023b1fecb05ab43b124081fa170eb8a04cde39c86811f2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-8e14f67b26df-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Jonathan S. Franklin (Petitioner), the petitioner asserts that the patent has led to multimillion\u2011dollar damages and an injunction prohibiting any testing company from conducting homocysteine tests by any method for any reason."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States Department of Justice",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "8e14f67b26df95ffae023b1fecb05ab43b124081fa170eb8a04cde39c86811f2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-8e14f67b26df-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The United States Department of Justice, as amicus, argues that claim 13 satisfies the written\u2011description, enablement, and definiteness requirements of \u00a7112 of the Patent Act."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
