              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Jonathan S. Franklin (Petitioner), according to Jonathan S. Franklin (Petitioner), according to Jonathan S. Franklin (Petitioner), the patent claim is infringed whenever any doctor looks at a homocysteine test result and reflexively thinks about a basic natural correlation."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "8e14f67b26df95ffae023b1fecb05ab43b124081fa170eb8a04cde39c86811f2",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-8e14f67b26df-0002-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 36,
                "start": 36
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, commercial laboratory companies like LabCorp are selling the test to practice our invention."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "8e14f67b26df95ffae023b1fecb05ab43b124081fa170eb8a04cde39c86811f2",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-8e14f67b26df-0002-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 39,
                "start": 39
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, anyone who makes, uses or sells the invention is potentially liable as an infringer."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Franklin",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "8e14f67b26df95ffae023b1fecb05ab43b124081fa170eb8a04cde39c86811f2",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-8e14f67b26df-0001-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 19,
                "start": 19
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Franklin, it applies to any homocysteine test, no matter how it\u2019s done, no matter what reason it\u2019s done, no matter if it\u2019s in the prior art, no matter if I invent it tomorrow."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Franklin",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "8e14f67b26df95ffae023b1fecb05ab43b124081fa170eb8a04cde39c86811f2",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-8e14f67b26df-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 20,
                "start": 20
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Franklin, so I don\u2019t think the Court needs to get into the inquiry, and I don\u2019t think the Patent Office really wants to get into that inquiry either."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner Position",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
